{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>And if to his son he designates her.</b> If the master wishes to designate her, no other act of kiddushin is required, but only the money of her acquisition, and he says to her: 'You are betrothed to me with the money your father received as your price.' And if he did not wish to designate her to himself but to his son — 'as the manner of the daughters he shall do to her': the master must give her from his own property as a dowry of virgins, for she is a daughter of Israel and the master stands in the place of her father. And the Scripture commanded in this matter just as it commanded concerning the gift given to a released slave, and all of it is kindness from the Holy One, blessed be He." "<b>Or</b> its meaning may be: 'as the manner of the daughters he shall do to her' — and what is the manner of the daughters? That if he takes another woman in addition to her mother, 'her food, her clothing, and her conjugal duty he shall not diminish' (Exodus 21:10)." "<b>And Rashi</b>, of blessed memory, explained: 'her food' (שארה) — this refers to maintenance; 'her clothing' (כסותה) — as its plain meaning; 'her duty' (עונתה) — conjugal relations. But the Ramban took issue with his interpretation and said: for what they said in Ketubot, 'this Tanna holds that maintenance is by Torah law,' as it is taught: 'שארה — these are maintenance,' as it is written (Psalms 78:27) ״וימטר עליהם כעפר שאר״ — this is certainly the position of an individual sage, and what emerges from the sugya of the Talmud is that the Rabbis enacted maintenance and it is not by Torah law. Therefore he, of blessed memory, explained that שארה means 'close flesh,' for שאר everywhere means flesh that is joined and close to a person's own flesh, from the language of (Leviticus 18:6) 'שאר בשרו,' and our Rabbis of blessed memory interpreted (Leviticus 21:2) 'כי אם לשארו' — this is his wife, as it is said (Genesis 2:24) ״ודבק באשתו והיו לבשר אחד״ — thus שארה is her close flesh. And כסותה is the clothing of his bed, as it is said (Exodus 22:26) 'כי היא כסותה לבדה' etc. — in what shall he lie? And עונתה is her appointed time when he comes to her at the time of intimacy, and this is 'the manner of the daughters.' And the reason is: the other woman shall not sit with him on the bed according to her honor so that they become one flesh while this one is with him as a concubine — he lies with her incidentally and on the ground, like one who comes to a prostitute. And so our Rabbis of blessed memory said: שארה — this is 'close flesh,' that he should not conduct himself with her by the custom of the Persians, who perform their marital relations in their garments; for it is the way of Scripture everywhere to speak of the marital bed in clean language. And these three matters are what a man has with his wife in union; and the maintenance and clothing of a woman are a rabbinic enactment."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:02:20.372784686Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}